WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 4: Places and Community.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.420
Welcome to Unit 4!

3
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:11.860
In this unit you will explore the places in
your community and the people who help you there.

4
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.020
You will learn to name places like the hospital,
the market, the court, the college and the garden,

5
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.060
and to talk about helpers like the
doctor, the officer and the sailor.

6
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:27.180
You will describe places using words like quiet
and busy, give clear instructions, ask questions,

7
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.040
and explain your ideas with the word “because”.

8
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.860
By the end, you will be ready to write your
own report about a place in your community —

9
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.360
just like Amal does in this unit's story.

10
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.560
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:49.080
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
places in your community and the people who work there.

12
00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.160
you will also describe a place using
adjectives and opposites, like quiet and busy.

13
00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:59.720
you will also give simple instructions using
imperatives (“exit the court quietly.”).

14
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.660
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.440
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
doctor, officer, sailor, hospital, court, college.

16
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.740
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.920
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.760
The reading sequence includes Our
Community and A Poem: “Places I Know”.

19
00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.320
Read actively.

20
00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.960
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.760
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.560
The first language focus is Imperatives (Giving Instructions).

23
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.420
An imperative is a special way to use a
verb to give a command or an instruction.

24
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.840
It tells someone to do something.

25
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:51.120
We need imperatives to give clear directions, like “Exit
the court quietly” or “Go to the hospital if you are sick.”

26
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.920
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

27
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.700
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — My Community.

28
00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.880
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

29
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.160
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

30
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.560
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

31
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.120
You are ready to begin.

32
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:20.320
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

33
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.820
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

34
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:27.680
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
